{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/summary_route.py","reason":"New leaf module: the exact-{summary} selector predicate and the OperationOutcome→result/error/synced-baseline mapping, extracted from dispatch_one (at 740 LOC) to respect the 800-LOC cap; the executor is called directly so the selected route bypasses the generic retry wrapper."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_handlers.py","reason":"Add the constructor-injected legacy-default summary_executor field to BatchApplyContext and the routing guard in handle_update that consumes terminal tags without false baseline/provenance advance."},{"path":"docs/adr/0103-reconciler-operation-coordination.md","reason":"Finalize the S1 lifecycle boundary naming S3 as sole production cutover, fuse/deferral consumer, and compatibility-bridge retirement owner."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_apply_handlers_operation_outcome.py","reason":"Held-out oracle: exact-vs-mixed routing, generic-retry poison bypass, terminal outcome mapping (one redacted ≤512-codepoint message, no baseline/provenance advance, batch continues), and the ADR-0103 S3-ownership assertion."}]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"FILE_IMPACT","timestamp":1787579999431659001,"uuid":"c15827ce-29aa-40bf-8e30-733d6af1aee9"}